Z||000001||theogre||08-18-2001||01:51 PM||||Jay, I imagine that Archie has looked at plenty of transmissions. I'll let him explain what he's found if anything...<P>What I've found along that line is that you are looking at a full custom job including higher grade cases to stuff. Problem is there are no higher grade cases because all the people like B&M and so on still mainly deal with inline RWD transmissions.<P>To change ratios beyond the OE sets is the same problem. The demand is too small for most of the people with the equipment to make them to justify the work.<P>To give you an idea,,, check the cost of the limited slip conversion for one of the Fiero transmissions... that one set of parts is $1000+.||||reg||1
